The Alfa-Business name and red A mark identify the banking context of the user-provided case.
This is an unofficial design prototype, not a production banking service.

Four anonymized company profiles, including revenue and payment relationship information, come from the user-provided demo_profiles.json.
News text, relevance scores, explanations, rules and suggested products are returned by the team's NewsAnalytics backend.
The backend currently seeds its news from the team's manually prepared golden_news.json.
Company display names describe the industry and are not legal names.
The supplied demo_profiles.json and feed_preview.xlsx are included in data/ for the team.
The web server serves dist/, forwards read-only /api/ requests to the configured backend, and handles server-only /api/ai/ analysis and chat requests.
Original source files in data/ are not served. News text is displayed with source attribution, without independent fact verification. Backend scores are preserved; the adapter replaces ambiguous supplier-concentration, PMI-direction and fuel-price rule wording with cautious profile-context notes.
Scores are not risk probabilities. Bank expertise and source links absent from the feed response are not invented by the website.
AI inference uses the organizer-provided OpenAI-compatible service at https://changellenge.up.railway.app/v1 with deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash by default. Model availability and team limits are controlled by the organizer. Authentication is server-only through LLM_API_KEY; no key is included in source files or browser code.
The application implements its own planning, allowlisted data tools, JSON validation, review/repair and cache. It uses built-in Node.js HTTP/fetch/crypto/filesystem APIs, without an external agent framework or model SDK.
Model-generated interpretations are separate from source news, deterministic relevance scores, and bank materials. Model review is not independent fact verification. Unverified prepared bank comments are not attributed to Alfa-Bank.
Live collection uses the official Bank of Russia RSS channel: https://www.cbr.ru/rss/RssPress. Source documents are retrieved over HTTPS; original text remains attributed to the publisher. Corpus search is limited to configured sources, not general internet search.
Three historical Alfa-Bank reports are supplied by the case materials folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15xZTLF1lZ65p6o5xpNA_fRbxjoV-UlG1. Only short page-verified quotations and document metadata/hashes are distributed in config/bank-excerpts.json; complete PDF files and rendered pages are not included in Git. These documents retain the bank's copyright; case access does not imply a redistribution licence.
The default reviewer is qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b through the same organizer API. Review by another model is not independent fact verification.
Server parsing dependencies (versions and transitive resolution are fixed in package.json/pnpm-lock.yaml): linkedom 0.18.14 (ISC, https://github.com/WebReflection/linkedom); fast-xml-parser 5.11.2 (MIT, https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser); pdfjs-dist 6.4.299 (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js). Dependencies include their upstream licence notices; optional PDF rendering support may install @napi-rs/canvas and its platform package.
data/quality-benchmark.json and automated-test content are synthetic examples authored for regression checks; their metrics are not an independent accuracy evaluation.
Local mode represents the owner of the local computer. Optional accounts, roles, company scopes and expert reviews are implemented by the application; production banking SSO is not integrated.
